WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.000
Each season of American Horror Story has been
unique from the rest, but there are still

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.820
some major common threads running throughout
the anthology installments that definitely

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.910
tie this hit thriller series together.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.769
Between recurring characters, locations, and
clever references scattered throughout, there

00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:19.320
are plenty of Easter eggs that connect all
six chapters of American Horror Story together.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.540
Familiar faces

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.060
The vast majority of the show's characters
have appeared in just one season each.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.750
But there have been a handful who've popped
back in later seasons.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.310
The first character to bridge the divide was
Pepper, who made her debut in Asylum as a

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:33.710
patient of Briarcliff Manor, who was committed
for killing her own child.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.800
In Freak Show, we got to see what transpired
before those events.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.890
We found out that poor Pepper was actually
a member of the Cabinet of Curiosities before

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.370
she was framed by her sister and brother-in-law
for the murder of their disfigured infant

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.430
Lucas.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:48.739
Sister Mary Eunice followed suit, which revealed
that there was more to her than the devilish

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:50.629
possession we saw in Asylum.

00:00:50.629 --> 00:00:53.199
Her return to Freak Show was much more pleasant
and subdued.

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:57.940
Dr. Arden, Marcy the realtor, Dr. Charles
Montgomery, and Queenie are some of the others

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.789
who've come back for another brief round of
nefarious fun.

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:03.700
But actress Sarah Paulson is the MVP of comebacks.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.470
Her celebrity psychic persona Billie Dean
Howard debuted in the first season, Murder

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.939
House, and returned for Season five's Hotel,
and her TV journalist alter ego Lana Winters

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:15.159
connected Asylum with the most recent season,
Roanoke.

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:16.610
Not just a name

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:19.979
There've also been several winks to characters
to link the stories together.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:23.930
Coven's Madison Montgomery, for example, may
have been related to the Murder House's original

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.840
owners, Charles and Nora Montgomery, if their
shared last name holds any significance.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.200
And attorney Harry Goodman from Season one
was probably related to Asylum's Sam Goodman,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.500
especially since they were both investigators.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.329
It's also probably no coincidence that there
were two characters named Jack Colquitt who

00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:40.640
were both detectives in different generations.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.750
In Roanoke, Edward Mott was the ancestor to
Freak Show's Dandy and Gloria Mott.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.130
Plus, those killer nurses from Murder House
came back into play in Roanoke as well.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:53.270
Chances are, the hunky Uber driver Rhett Snow
might have also had some kind of connection

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.960
to Coven character Myrtle Snow … unless
his name was actually a nod to Game of Thrones'

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.159
undead hero.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:00.240
But that'd just be crazy, right?

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.869
Theoretical throwbacks

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:05.840
Even where names and actual role reprisals
fail to appear, there are still some characters

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.999
that draw us back to something familiar from
the past.

00:02:07.999 --> 00:02:12.290
For example, Roanoke's Woods Witch is rumored
to be the original Supreme from Coven.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.170
And let's not forget that Cricket said he
was trained in New Orleans, which is where

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.959
the actor's other American Horror Story persona
spent some time during Coven.

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:23.200
Plus, Billie Dean made a direct mention of
the Roanoke colony all the way back in Murder

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.200
House.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.850
Meanwhile, it's widely believed that Oliver
Thredson from Asylum was actually the faceless

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.349
therapist that treated Dandy Mott in Freak
Show.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:34.150
And it's probably no coincidence that the
new season included all the pig masks after

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:38.120
Season one's Derrick harped on his pigman
fears so hard.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.610
Running rules

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.370
Another common thread found throughout all
six seasons lies in the supernatural rules

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:44.370
in play.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:48.720
Ghosts, for example, continually exist as
haunting, visible presences that appear to

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.610
be confined to the locations of their death
— but can have physical, and sometimes deadly,

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.510
interactions with the living around them.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:58.390
Spirit mediums are also regularly brought
into play, and witchcraft is obviously a very

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.030
real practice throughout the series.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.750
Demonic possessions run rampant throughout
the show, and multiple installments feature

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.510
vampires' thirst for blood.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:08.879
All together, these shared mythologies make
up the sinister backbone of the whole body

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:11.819
of the show, and every season relies on them.

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:13.040
Thematic threads

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.209
That's not all that bleeds together about
American Horror Story's seasons.

00:03:16.209 --> 00:03:19.670
There's also the common themes behind the
various characters' motives and actions.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.000
Mommy issues seem to loom large for a lot
of the men on the show, and there have been

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.190
several women who killed off their husbands
along the way as well.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:30.270
Bigamy is another big one — just how many
girlfriends did Evan Peters' characters have

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.270
anyway?

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.489
And let's not forget how pop culture-obsessed
so many of Sarah Paulson's characters have

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:35.489
been.

00:03:35.489 --> 00:03:37.020
Speaking of which ...

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.769
Visual cues

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:42.579
It's no mistake that some seasons of American
Horror Story have given fans a sense of deja

00:03:42.579 --> 00:03:43.939
vu.

00:03:43.939 --> 00:03:46.879
Several of the camera angles throughout have
been set up as direct references to stories

00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:51.079
past — like the repeat opening scenes from
Murder House and Roanoke, and all that time

00:03:51.079 --> 00:03:53.189
the cameras spent looking at staircases.

00:03:53.189 --> 00:03:56.950
Eagle-eyed fans might have also spotted the
Roanoke Butcher's cleaver and some other throwback

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.290
weapons among those that were laid out in
Hotel.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.590
And even the element of literally two-faced
characters — like Bette and Dot from Freak

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:05.480
Show and Edward Mordrake — seem to have
foreshadowed what would later come for the

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.250
cast members portraying them.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:12.090
After all, Sarah Paulson's appearance in multiple
roles in the subsequent seasons Hotel and

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.780
Roanoke could be a tribute to her ability
to double up.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:19.220
And Wes Bentley's Hotel character certainly
had two minds pushing and pulling his behaviors,

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.220
right?

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.489
Sinful significance

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:24.889
One of the biggest takeaways that seems to
come through with American Horror Story is

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:27.250
its grander statement on the concept of sin.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:31.610
A lot of fans think the individual seasons
represent the layers of hell in Dante's Inferno,

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:34.190
while others think they're each playing on
the seven deadly sins.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.289
Both sides seem to have some basis in the
show's reality.

00:04:37.289 --> 00:04:40.790
Murder House, for example, involved a lot
of bedroom behavior by its characters, so

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:45.470
it might fall under the "lust" category, and
Asylum was filled with fraud and false witness.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.750
Coven had heresy written all over it, and
Freak Show dealt a lot with the concept of

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:49.750
pride.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:53.740
Hotel, meanwhile, was all about wrath and
gluttony, and Roanoke had more than one instance

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.860
of adultery and coveting…not to mention,
tons of violence.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.510
The fact that Hotel included an actual Ten
Commandments Killer even seemed like a giant

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.340
nod to these longheld theories.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.720
Whether or not the future seasons continue
to correspond to these wicked markers remains

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.720
to be seen.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.180
But one thing's for sure, there's a bigger
picture here that's only beginning to reveal

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.180
itself…

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:12.180
Thanks for watching!

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.900
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.780
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

